1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kissasia.net =

2
00:00:03,726 --> 00:00:06,766
- Big smiles, please. - Cheese.

3
00:00:08,706 --> 00:00:10,206
You look so beautiful.

4
00:00:10,306 --> 00:00:12,106
Oh, you're the best.

5
00:00:18,646 --> 00:00:19,676
What?

6
00:00:22,486 --> 00:00:23,946
We should wrap things up now.

7
00:00:24,016 --> 00:00:26,486
I'll pack up, so you can head out first.

8
00:00:26,616 --> 00:00:28,486
Okay, break time, okay.

9
00:00:28,626 --> 00:00:30,726
Honey, it's so cold.

10
00:00:56,516 --> 00:00:57,846
Hey, let go of me!

11
00:00:58,186 --> 00:00:59,256
Stay still!

12
00:01:00,986 --> 00:01:02,686
- Calm down! - Do you want to die?

13
00:01:20,106 --> 00:01:21,536
- Get out, you punk. - I'm not getting out, you bastards.

14
00:01:21,606 --> 00:01:22,746
Hey, you guys.

15
00:01:24,306 --> 00:01:25,916
Who are you? Let go of me.

16
00:01:25,976 --> 00:01:28,646
Who are you guys? You've got the wrong person.

17
00:01:30,086 --> 00:01:31,086
Where is this?

18
00:01:31,386 --> 00:01:33,216
- Where am I? Who are you people? - Ji Won Ho.

19
00:01:35,786 --> 00:01:36,856
You...

20
00:01:36,856 --> 00:01:38,356
What do you think you're doing?

21
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,226
Hee Ju...

22
00:01:43,496 --> 00:01:44,496
Hee Ju...

23
00:01:52,076 --> 00:01:53,676
Just trust me.

24
00:01:54,236 --> 00:01:57,276
I promise I'll make it back in one piece.

25
00:02:01,816 --> 00:02:03,016
Hee Ju.

26
00:02:03,016 --> 00:02:04,216
Hee Ju!

27
00:02:13,056 --> 00:02:14,196
Let's go fulfill...

28
00:02:15,226 --> 00:02:16,266
that promise.

29
00:02:16,626 --> 00:02:17,666
Wait a minute!

30
00:02:19,096 --> 00:02:20,236
I'm getting a divorce soon,

31
00:02:20,596 --> 00:02:22,036
and once things are over between Mi Young and me,

32
00:02:22,106 --> 00:02:24,366
you'll have your chance with her, Calvin.

33
00:02:24,366 --> 00:02:26,136
Aren't you jumping the gun?

34
00:02:29,506 --> 00:02:31,006
- Let's go. - Hey!

35
00:02:31,406 --> 00:02:32,776
Let go of me, you bastards!

36
00:02:33,416 --> 00:02:34,416
Hey.

37
00:02:37,246 --> 00:02:38,246
Hee Ju.

38
00:02:39,456 --> 00:02:40,456
Hee Ju.

39
00:02:40,986 --> 00:02:44,086
Are you okay? Hee Ju. Oh no...

40
00:02:46,096 --> 00:02:47,696
Just hang in there.

41
00:02:53,596 --> 00:02:56,366
Do you think you'll get away with this, you bastards?

42
00:03:03,306 --> 00:03:04,346
And where is this place?

43
00:03:05,106 --> 00:03:07,546
What kind of stunt are you pulling on me now?

44
00:03:10,246 --> 00:03:11,486
This is my vacation home.

45
00:03:13,186 --> 00:03:14,186
Vacation home?

46
00:03:14,656 --> 00:03:15,826
The view isn't bad, is it?

47
00:03:16,586 --> 00:03:20,026
This is where my grandparents lived until they passed away.

48
00:03:20,796 --> 00:03:23,526
I come here to rest sometimes when I need to recharge.

49
00:03:25,126 --> 00:03:28,296
Then you should have come alone. I don't need to recharge.

50
00:03:35,446 --> 00:03:36,506
I wanted to,

51
00:03:37,806 --> 00:03:38,876
at least once,

52
00:03:39,946 --> 00:03:43,286
open up and tell you my deepest thoughts.

53
00:03:43,986 --> 00:03:45,586
Then you should have just said so from the beginning.

54
00:03:45,586 --> 00:03:47,986
Did you really have to put on such a violent show for this?

55
00:03:48,356 --> 00:03:51,456
We'll see if it ends as just a show after we talk.

56
00:03:53,726 --> 00:03:56,666
Don't be too nervous. I'm not trying to scare you.

57
00:03:57,066 --> 00:03:58,936
You say that after scaring me half to death.

58
00:04:00,196 --> 00:04:02,566
So what is this deep talk you wanted to have?

59
00:04:04,506 --> 00:04:07,906
If that incident hadn't happened seven years ago,

60
00:04:09,006 --> 00:04:13,516
I never would have let Mi Young go.

61
00:04:18,116 --> 00:04:19,116
Hee Ju.

62
00:04:20,116 --> 00:04:24,126
Luckily, the doctor said it's not a major fracture or injury.

63
00:04:24,726 --> 00:04:26,796
You'll be fine after a few days of rest,

64
00:04:26,856 --> 00:04:28,096
so don't worry too much.

65
00:04:28,726 --> 00:04:30,966
Still, it's a huge relief it wasn't worse.

66
00:04:31,496 --> 00:04:32,736
They tried to kill me.

67
00:04:34,666 --> 00:04:36,366
Someone pushed me...

68
00:04:38,706 --> 00:04:39,836
off the cliff.

69
00:04:40,836 --> 00:04:42,646
Hee Ju, what are you saying?

70
00:04:43,146 --> 00:04:44,606
Who would push you?

71
00:04:44,706 --> 00:04:47,076
It's true. I'm telling you, it's true!

72
00:04:47,716 --> 00:04:49,946
Someone definitely pushed me.

73
00:04:58,726 --> 00:04:59,726
I'm sure of it.

74
00:05:01,196 --> 00:05:02,826
It's still so clear.

75
00:05:03,996 --> 00:05:07,796
The feeling of someone's hands pushing my back.

76
00:05:13,336 --> 00:05:15,276
But still, that doesn't make any sense.

77
00:05:15,336 --> 00:05:17,776
Who would do such a terrible thing to you?

78
00:05:19,516 --> 00:05:20,946
I have my suspicions...

79
00:05:22,886 --> 00:05:24,116
as to who I think it was.

80
00:05:27,416 --> 00:05:28,486
Calvin.

81
00:05:30,186 --> 00:05:31,386
It was Calvin.

82
00:05:32,226 --> 00:05:33,526
He's the one who tried to kill me.

83
00:05:33,926 --> 00:05:34,926
What?

84
00:05:35,356 --> 00:05:37,926
What basis do you have for saying that?

85
00:05:37,996 --> 00:05:41,696
Calvin is the type of person who, when I said I was dating CEO Ji,

86
00:05:42,366 --> 00:05:44,766
fired me on the spot without a second thought.

87
00:05:46,276 --> 00:05:48,506
He can do anything he sets his mind to.

88
00:05:49,246 --> 00:05:51,876
He has the power and influence to do whatever he wants.

89
00:05:54,076 --> 00:05:55,446
Who else could it be but Calvin?

90
00:05:58,716 --> 00:06:00,686
Think about it, CEO Baek.

91
00:06:02,256 --> 00:06:03,256
Calvin...

92
00:06:04,256 --> 00:06:06,496
is much scarier than you think.

93
00:06:14,766 --> 00:06:15,866
Is that true?

94
00:06:17,806 --> 00:06:19,376
So your son, no...

95
00:06:20,076 --> 00:06:23,306
The child you believed was your son turned out not to be yours?

96
00:06:25,446 --> 00:06:26,746
How is that possible?

97
00:06:27,516 --> 00:06:28,716
When did you find that out?

98
00:06:29,446 --> 00:06:30,486
Three years ago.

99
00:06:31,286 --> 00:06:32,656
Three years ago?

100
00:06:33,616 --> 00:06:35,386
But I heard you only got divorced recently.

101
00:06:35,786 --> 00:06:38,656
I fought a lawsuit for three years to get custody of the child.

102
00:06:40,396 --> 00:06:41,826
But I ended up losing the case.

103
00:06:44,466 --> 00:06:45,596
Three years ago,

104
00:06:46,736 --> 00:06:50,136
the day the detailed test results came back negative for paternity,

105
00:06:51,206 --> 00:06:53,476
I happened to see Mi Young at the hospital.

106
00:06:55,076 --> 00:06:57,176
She looked pregnant.

107
00:06:58,546 --> 00:07:00,216
I couldn't bring myself to say hello,

108
00:07:01,176 --> 00:07:02,946
and just watched her from a distance.

109
00:07:04,586 --> 00:07:05,616
Honestly,

110
00:07:07,186 --> 00:07:08,516
it was a truly bitter feeling.

111
00:07:13,396 --> 00:07:14,396
I, too,

112
00:07:17,396 --> 00:07:19,836
couldn't protect my child in the end.

113
00:07:21,236 --> 00:07:22,706
I haven't given up yet.

114
00:07:24,466 --> 00:07:26,076
The child I raised as my own,

115
00:07:26,576 --> 00:07:30,046
I will get him back, no matter how long it takes.

116
00:07:32,746 --> 00:07:35,076
Calvin, are you telling me this because?

117
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:37,216
I have absolutely no ulterior motives...

118
00:07:37,286 --> 00:07:38,586
or feelings for Mi Young.

119
00:07:41,316 --> 00:07:44,926
So if you're seeing Hee Ju out of resentment toward me,

120
00:07:46,796 --> 00:07:48,356
I'm asking you to stop right there.

121
00:07:57,236 --> 00:07:59,436
It's okay. I don't have an appetite.

122
00:07:59,736 --> 00:08:02,376
Still, have a bite. You need to eat to take your pills.

123
00:08:03,376 --> 00:08:04,576
What about CEO Ji?

124
00:08:05,946 --> 00:08:07,716
Why isn't CEO Ji here yet?

125
00:08:08,716 --> 00:08:11,216
I sent him a text. He'll come once he sees it.

126
00:08:12,616 --> 00:08:14,156
Are you sure you sent him a message?

127
00:08:14,986 --> 00:08:19,526
You didn't just say that without telling him, did you?

128
00:08:20,726 --> 00:08:23,966
If you really don't believe me, text him yourself.

129
00:08:30,236 --> 00:08:31,306
CEO Ji!

130
00:08:41,316 --> 00:08:43,746
Where have you been?

131
00:08:43,916 --> 00:08:45,786
I was waiting forever.

132
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:50,556
Are you okay? Are you badly hurt?

133
00:08:51,486 --> 00:08:53,956
I thought I was going to die.

134
00:08:59,996 --> 00:09:02,866
Look, I got a big scrape here.

135
00:09:03,106 --> 00:09:06,276
I'm just glad it's not worse. Hurry and eat something.

136
00:09:06,406 --> 00:09:08,736
I don't have an appetite, and my wrist hurts...

137
00:09:08,806 --> 00:09:11,346
- You have to eat to get better. - My hand hurts. Can't you feed me?

138
00:09:11,406 --> 00:09:14,276
Oh, come on. Just eat. Here, I'll pour you some water.

139
00:09:19,286 --> 00:09:20,916
You found Hee Ju, right?

140
00:09:22,686 --> 00:09:23,726
You went through a lot.

141
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:28,926
Where were you all day? I couldn't reach you.

142
00:09:30,066 --> 00:09:32,636
Is it that hard to send one message...

143
00:09:33,036 --> 00:09:35,066
if you can't come, or if you're going to be late?

144
00:09:35,066 --> 00:09:36,636
It's not like you were kidnapped.

145
00:09:37,766 --> 00:09:38,866
How did you know?

146
00:09:39,736 --> 00:09:43,076
- What? - I just came from seeing Calvin.

147
00:09:45,106 --> 00:09:46,216
I heard everything.

148
00:09:46,876 --> 00:09:48,346
I know why Calvin got a divorce.

149
00:09:48,776 --> 00:09:49,816
Calvin...

150
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:54,656
told you that himself?

151
00:09:55,286 --> 00:09:57,086
I guess all this time...

152
00:09:58,826 --> 00:10:00,456
I've really misjudged him.

153
00:10:01,796 --> 00:10:04,226
And I did a lot of thinking on the way over,

154
00:10:05,366 --> 00:10:08,696
and I think I've been rash about a lot of things.

155
00:10:09,736 --> 00:10:12,406
I'll take care of Hee Ju until she gets discharged.

156
00:10:15,036 --> 00:10:17,806
And that written pledge...

157
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:22,846
Let's just forget about it.

158
00:10:23,616 --> 00:10:25,816
I'll take care of everything.

159
00:10:26,516 --> 00:10:27,956
So Hee Ju was right.

160
00:10:29,726 --> 00:10:31,026
Hee Ju said...

161
00:10:32,156 --> 00:10:33,896
that Calvin was a dangerous man.

162
00:10:35,196 --> 00:10:36,926
I mean, how could you change your mind...

163
00:10:37,396 --> 00:10:38,996
just because of what Calvin said?

164
00:10:39,296 --> 00:10:42,366
No, it's not like I changed my mind just because of that.

165
00:10:44,366 --> 00:10:48,406
Anyway, I'm leaving. Take good care of Hee Ju.

166
00:10:50,046 --> 00:10:51,446
He's a lot like you.

167
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:56,486
Calvin.

168
00:10:57,786 --> 00:10:59,956
He said he was desperate to get his child back.

169
00:11:02,656 --> 00:11:05,796
And it suddenly made me think of you.

170
00:11:07,456 --> 00:11:08,796
I hate to admit it,

171
00:11:09,726 --> 00:11:10,766
but you two...

172
00:11:13,736 --> 00:11:14,836
are a lot alike.

173
00:11:15,066 --> 00:11:16,736
What's your point?

174
00:11:17,506 --> 00:11:20,036
Honestly, I never really understood...

175
00:11:20,106 --> 00:11:22,136
why you used to like a guy like that.

176
00:11:23,946 --> 00:11:25,006
But...

177
00:11:26,816 --> 00:11:28,176
now I think...

178
00:11:30,616 --> 00:11:31,986
I kind of get it.

179
00:11:39,026 --> 00:11:40,896
I'm sorry it took me so long...

180
00:11:43,396 --> 00:11:44,826
to understand, Mi Young.

181
00:12:03,146 --> 00:12:04,186
Did you hear?

182
00:12:04,886 --> 00:12:08,316
CEO Ji is busy taking care of his young girlfriend,

183
00:12:08,486 --> 00:12:10,456
so he's stuck to her like glue.

184
00:12:11,326 --> 00:12:13,756
Well, that's over as of today.

185
00:12:14,456 --> 00:12:16,766
- What? - She's being discharged today.

186
00:12:17,226 --> 00:12:20,096
So, are they coming here together later?

187
00:12:20,236 --> 00:12:22,236
Why would they come here together?

188
00:12:22,336 --> 00:12:25,536
His girlfriend's a writer for our company, you know.

189
00:12:25,606 --> 00:12:26,636
She's an official employee.

190
00:12:26,736 --> 00:12:28,176
You call that being an official employee?

191
00:12:28,236 --> 00:12:29,376
It was pure nepotism.

192
00:12:29,706 --> 00:12:30,876
And I'm dead set against...

193
00:12:31,246 --> 00:12:33,516
that woman coming back to this company.

194
00:12:34,876 --> 00:12:36,886
All because of one woman, the CEO of a company...

195
00:12:37,686 --> 00:12:39,686
How many days has he been away from the office?

196
00:12:46,496 --> 00:12:49,566
He doesn't pull any punches.

197
00:12:50,196 --> 00:12:53,366
He really keeps business and personal matters separate.

198
00:12:53,966 --> 00:12:55,396
Now that his affair is out in the open,

199
00:12:55,736 --> 00:12:57,306
it's game over for him.

200
00:12:59,706 --> 00:13:01,406
We don't even need the Domestic Affairs Investigation.

201
00:13:01,836 --> 00:13:03,746
We should ride this momentum and just...

202
00:13:04,706 --> 00:13:06,146
go straight to trial.

203
00:13:11,946 --> 00:13:14,786
Affairs are my specialty,

204
00:13:15,486 --> 00:13:18,686
and no one I've ever caught for it has ever gotten away with it.

205
00:13:19,826 --> 00:13:23,266
He said he was going to end things with her.

206
00:13:24,066 --> 00:13:26,436
Who did? Your husband?

207
00:13:26,796 --> 00:13:28,266
I'm not sure,

208
00:13:30,506 --> 00:13:32,136
but I don't think he was serious...

209
00:13:32,136 --> 00:13:33,476
about being in a relationship with her.

210
00:13:33,806 --> 00:13:35,336
Let me tell you,

211
00:13:35,776 --> 00:13:39,006
nobody ever plans to have an affair.

212
00:13:39,576 --> 00:13:40,746
Looking back,

213
00:13:41,546 --> 00:13:43,246
I think it was because of what happened.

214
00:13:44,686 --> 00:13:45,686
That day...

215
00:13:47,156 --> 00:13:50,126
when I found out about his pain.

216
00:13:52,626 --> 00:13:55,496
The very fact that I knew about it...

217
00:13:56,196 --> 00:13:57,626
must have made him really uncomfortable.

218
00:13:59,766 --> 00:14:02,036
He was so uncomfortable and bothered by it...

219
00:14:03,536 --> 00:14:05,506
that he acted out in rebellion.

220
00:14:06,006 --> 00:14:08,676
Deciding to start dating in the middle of a lawsuit...

221
00:14:08,736 --> 00:14:10,406
was your husband's choice.

222
00:14:10,646 --> 00:14:12,406
It's not like you pushed him into it, Mi Young.

223
00:14:13,546 --> 00:14:16,586
Don't get too hung up on these petty feelings.

224
00:14:17,546 --> 00:14:19,046
Let's remember why we started this.

225
00:14:20,856 --> 00:14:23,226
Why you, Mi Young,

226
00:14:23,986 --> 00:14:25,656
decided to get a divorce in the first place.

227
00:14:30,226 --> 00:14:33,866
(Maesan Hospital)

228
00:14:39,706 --> 00:14:40,706
What?

229
00:14:41,376 --> 00:14:42,436
I'm being discharged today.

230
00:14:43,006 --> 00:14:45,276
What? A discharge party?

231
00:14:46,946 --> 00:14:47,946
I can't.

232
00:14:48,716 --> 00:14:51,886
My boyfriend said he was picking me up today.

233
00:14:53,886 --> 00:14:55,256
I'll introduce you later.

234
00:14:57,756 --> 00:14:59,596
Hey, I'll call you later. Bye.

235
00:15:17,346 --> 00:15:19,916
I'll call you a taxi, so tell me your address.

236
00:15:20,216 --> 00:15:23,986
Did CEO Ji really send you in his place?

237
00:15:24,316 --> 00:15:26,816
Why else would I have come all this way?

238
00:15:29,356 --> 00:15:30,356
That's so cruel.

239
00:15:30,626 --> 00:15:32,796
How could he not even show up on the day I'm discharged?

240
00:15:33,026 --> 00:15:35,896
He won't be showing up from now on, either.

241
00:15:36,526 --> 00:15:37,526
What did you say?

242
00:15:37,696 --> 00:15:38,696
Won Ho...

243
00:15:39,636 --> 00:15:41,096
isn't going to see you anymore, Hee Ju.

244
00:15:42,496 --> 00:15:43,506
What?

245
00:15:43,836 --> 00:15:45,736
How could you be so heartless?

246
00:15:46,406 --> 00:15:48,606
Breaking up with her like that.

247
00:15:50,146 --> 00:15:53,476
- That young woman must be furious. - I had no choice.

248
00:15:53,746 --> 00:15:55,376
This is the only way to end things.

249
00:15:55,546 --> 00:15:57,016
I don't know...

250
00:15:57,586 --> 00:15:59,756
I don't think it'll be that easy.

251
00:16:00,256 --> 00:16:02,886
That desperation to be by your side,

252
00:16:02,886 --> 00:16:04,926
even if she had to pretend to be your girlfriend...

253
00:16:04,926 --> 00:16:07,096
Do you think feelings like that just vanish overnight?

254
00:16:07,556 --> 00:16:09,156
How do you know so much?

255
00:16:09,226 --> 00:16:11,226
Coming from the man who learned about love from books.

256
00:16:11,226 --> 00:16:12,626
What's that supposed to mean?

257
00:16:12,796 --> 00:16:15,496
I'll have you know I graduated from Hankuk University.

258
00:16:15,966 --> 00:16:16,966
Gosh.

259
00:16:17,666 --> 00:16:20,176
Anyway, it's completely over now.

260
00:16:20,936 --> 00:16:22,176
If you say so,

261
00:16:23,006 --> 00:16:24,746
we'll just have to wait and see.

262
00:16:26,946 --> 00:16:28,646
Every single day, it's these paper cups.

263
00:16:34,786 --> 00:16:35,786
Anyway,

264
00:16:36,586 --> 00:16:38,926
the biggest hurdle left for you...

265
00:16:39,826 --> 00:16:41,096
is the Domestic Affairs Investigation.

266
00:16:41,696 --> 00:16:42,796
The Domestic Affairs Investigation?

267
00:16:43,196 --> 00:16:46,066
These investigators are all sharp, just like me.

268
00:16:46,596 --> 00:16:48,996
Provoking hotheads like you...

269
00:16:49,066 --> 00:16:52,006
until you show your true colours is a piece of cake for them.

270
00:16:52,106 --> 00:16:54,276
What's wrong with my temper?

271
00:16:54,336 --> 00:16:55,806
See? You can't even hold it in for a second.

272
00:16:55,876 --> 00:16:56,876
Good grief.

273
00:16:57,676 --> 00:16:59,006
Domestic Affairs Investigation or whatever,

274
00:16:59,076 --> 00:17:01,446
I'm done fighting with Mi Young.

275
00:17:01,816 --> 00:17:03,316
I'm just going to let things run their course.

276
00:17:03,586 --> 00:17:04,716
Dragging out this lawsuit...

277
00:17:04,786 --> 00:17:06,016
will just drain us both.

278
00:17:06,256 --> 00:17:07,256
So...

279
00:17:07,386 --> 00:17:09,726
are you going to give them everything they want and end it?

280
00:17:09,886 --> 00:17:13,596
Of course not. I have a line I won't cross.

281
00:17:14,856 --> 00:17:17,066
They won't cross that line, will they?

282
00:17:17,466 --> 00:17:18,466
Listen.

283
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:20,766
You know who the opposing counsel is, don't you?

284
00:17:20,766 --> 00:17:21,796
I do.

285
00:17:21,936 --> 00:17:23,766
Jeon Chi Hyun. Once she bites, she never lets go.

286
00:17:23,906 --> 00:17:26,406
So don't you let your guard down until the very end.

287
00:17:26,506 --> 00:17:28,976
Let your guard down for a second, and she'll cross the line...

288
00:17:29,036 --> 00:17:30,706
and take you for everything you've got.

289
00:17:36,186 --> 00:17:37,186
Okay.

290
00:17:40,286 --> 00:17:42,286
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

291
00:17:47,356 --> 00:17:48,356
Calvin.

292
00:17:49,296 --> 00:17:50,666
It was Calvin.

293
00:17:51,596 --> 00:17:52,996
He's the one who tried to kill me.

294
00:17:56,836 --> 00:17:57,836
No.

295
00:17:59,006 --> 00:18:00,736
There's no way Calvin would do that.

296
00:18:02,406 --> 00:18:03,446
Manipulate?

297
00:18:03,976 --> 00:18:05,746
I am actually holding myself back.

298
00:18:06,846 --> 00:18:10,846
All I want is for Mi Young to be happy.

299
00:18:12,416 --> 00:18:13,586
You know, Mi Young...

300
00:18:14,816 --> 00:18:15,916
If by any chance...

301
00:18:16,556 --> 00:18:18,186
If you're ever having a hard time...

302
00:18:19,426 --> 00:18:21,456
He can do anything he sets his mind to.

303
00:18:22,496 --> 00:18:25,066
He has the power and influence to do whatever he wants.

304
00:18:26,236 --> 00:18:27,666
Who else could it be but Calvin?

305
00:18:32,166 --> 00:18:35,536
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

306
00:18:35,606 --> 00:18:38,276
(Calvin)

307
00:18:43,946 --> 00:18:46,586
It's me. By any chance,

308
00:18:47,086 --> 00:18:48,656
are you free this evening?

309
00:19:06,536 --> 00:19:09,206
But why is it so empty?

310
00:19:10,676 --> 00:19:11,676
It is, isn't it?

311
00:19:11,976 --> 00:19:13,316
Why are there no customers today?

312
00:19:14,046 --> 00:19:15,046
Don't tell me...

313
00:19:15,316 --> 00:19:17,346
you turned away customers because of me, did you?

314
00:19:17,786 --> 00:19:18,816
Of course not.

315
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:21,156
I may not look like it, but I'm a businessman.

316
00:19:24,786 --> 00:19:25,786
Let's eat.

317
00:19:32,866 --> 00:19:34,796
I'm sorry, but we're fully booked tonight.

318
00:19:36,906 --> 00:19:39,206
The chef said he prepared something special,

319
00:19:39,606 --> 00:19:41,036
so I hope you like it.

320
00:19:47,816 --> 00:19:48,816
It's delicious.

321
00:19:49,716 --> 00:19:50,886
It's really delicious.

322
00:19:51,146 --> 00:19:52,146
I'm glad.

323
00:19:52,956 --> 00:19:53,956
Oh, right.

324
00:19:54,116 --> 00:19:56,156
You said you had something to tell me when you called.

325
00:19:56,526 --> 00:19:57,686
May I ask what it was?

326
00:20:00,926 --> 00:20:01,926
Well...

327
00:20:03,826 --> 00:20:06,536
A little while ago, Hee Ju went on an outdoor shoot...

328
00:20:06,596 --> 00:20:07,996
and had an accident.

329
00:20:08,696 --> 00:20:10,366
She slipped and fell from a cliff.

330
00:20:10,936 --> 00:20:11,936
Really?

331
00:20:12,606 --> 00:20:15,376
That sounds serious. Is she all right now?

332
00:20:17,146 --> 00:20:18,146
Yes.

333
00:20:19,446 --> 00:20:20,446
But...

334
00:20:21,376 --> 00:20:22,776
she mentioned you.

335
00:20:23,816 --> 00:20:24,816
Me?

336
00:20:25,086 --> 00:20:28,316
Hee Ju thinks she got hurt because of you.

337
00:20:30,426 --> 00:20:32,526
Oh, I see.

338
00:20:34,896 --> 00:20:36,196
That's not true, is it?

339
00:20:39,736 --> 00:20:40,736
Right?

340
00:20:40,966 --> 00:20:44,306
You're not the kind of person who would hurt Hee Ju.

341
00:20:45,006 --> 00:20:46,976
If I'd really been serious about it,

342
00:20:47,976 --> 00:20:48,976
she...

343
00:20:49,536 --> 00:20:50,606
would be dead.

344
00:20:53,716 --> 00:20:56,076
But that won't happen anymore.

345
00:20:57,046 --> 00:20:59,916
Everything's going to be all right now, Mi Young.

346
00:21:02,656 --> 00:21:03,656
Let's eat.

347
00:21:24,206 --> 00:21:25,506
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

348
00:21:28,246 --> 00:21:30,046
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

349
00:21:30,586 --> 00:21:31,686
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

350
00:21:42,696 --> 00:21:44,796
(15 Missed Calls: Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

351
00:21:54,706 --> 00:21:56,476
Are you really not going to answer?

352
00:21:57,176 --> 00:21:59,106
I only need a moment. Just one minute.

353
00:21:59,446 --> 00:22:01,046
This is so unfair.

354
00:22:01,576 --> 00:22:03,216
What did I do wrong?

355
00:22:05,116 --> 00:22:06,956
Let's not do this, Hee Ju.

356
00:22:12,486 --> 00:22:14,996
- You were home. - Yes, hey...

357
00:22:17,026 --> 00:22:18,026
Have you had dinner?

358
00:22:18,396 --> 00:22:20,166
Yes, I had dinner.

359
00:22:20,896 --> 00:22:21,896
What about you?

360
00:22:22,136 --> 00:22:24,266
Yes, I ate something too.

361
00:22:31,146 --> 00:22:32,646
Shouldn't you get that?

362
00:22:32,876 --> 00:22:34,716
No, it's fine. Don't worry about it.

363
00:22:55,766 --> 00:22:57,306
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

364
00:23:09,516 --> 00:23:10,516
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

365
00:23:13,456 --> 00:23:14,886
(Block Contact)

366
00:23:16,626 --> 00:23:17,626
(Block)

367
00:23:26,936 --> 00:23:28,736
Gosh, seriously.

368
00:23:34,276 --> 00:23:36,376
The person you are calling is unavailable...

369
00:23:37,706 --> 00:23:40,416
You really shouldn't have done that.

370
00:23:47,716 --> 00:23:48,716
Yes.

371
00:23:49,316 --> 00:23:50,786
Can we meet right now?

372
00:24:00,866 --> 00:24:02,096
Are you the one who called?

373
00:24:04,106 --> 00:24:05,236
Don't worry.

374
00:24:05,506 --> 00:24:07,276
I guarantee complete confidentiality.

375
00:24:10,176 --> 00:24:11,176
Let's see it.

376
00:24:18,016 --> 00:24:19,386
No way.

377
00:24:20,116 --> 00:24:21,116
How much do you want?

378
00:24:21,716 --> 00:24:23,926
I don't need any money.

379
00:24:24,186 --> 00:24:26,596
What? Then what do you want?

380
00:24:27,326 --> 00:24:28,326
Hey.

381
00:24:28,726 --> 00:24:32,866
If you just leave, that's a sweet deal for me.

382
00:24:51,846 --> 00:24:53,086
- Hey... - Listen...

383
00:24:56,456 --> 00:24:57,526
You go first.

384
00:24:58,686 --> 00:25:01,096
No. You go first.

385
00:25:03,526 --> 00:25:04,896
You heard, right?

386
00:25:05,066 --> 00:25:07,066
About the upcoming Domestic Affairs Investigation.

387
00:25:08,336 --> 00:25:10,006
Yes, I heard.

388
00:25:13,936 --> 00:25:17,876
Both of us are exhausted from the legal briefs.

389
00:25:18,676 --> 00:25:20,246
For the Domestic Affairs Investigation...

390
00:25:20,316 --> 00:25:21,916
So you're saying we shouldn't be so on edge...

391
00:25:21,976 --> 00:25:23,616
and just take it easy.

392
00:25:24,886 --> 00:25:27,656
Okay, I get it. I'll do that. Don't worry too much.

393
00:25:28,916 --> 00:25:29,956
Thank you.

394
00:25:30,986 --> 00:25:33,926
By the way, was Hee Ju discharged okay?

395
00:25:34,456 --> 00:25:35,456
Yes.

396
00:25:36,256 --> 00:25:37,326
And...

397
00:25:38,526 --> 00:25:40,966
there won't be any more trouble from now on.

398
00:25:41,136 --> 00:25:42,136
Okay.

399
00:25:48,506 --> 00:25:50,776
- Yes, A Ri. - Yes, Kyung Tae.

400
00:25:52,306 --> 00:25:54,346
- What do you mean? - What?

401
00:26:04,356 --> 00:26:05,756
("Falling in Love Isn't a Crime!")

402
00:26:05,826 --> 00:26:07,196
CEO Baek.

403
00:26:07,626 --> 00:26:09,256
What in the world is this?

404
00:26:09,626 --> 00:26:10,626
I don't know.

405
00:26:10,996 --> 00:26:12,866
It looks like someone secretly and maliciously took the photo...

406
00:26:12,866 --> 00:26:14,136
and sent it in.

407
00:26:14,196 --> 00:26:16,766
So what psycho would do this?

408
00:26:18,166 --> 00:26:19,606
But this photo,

409
00:26:19,936 --> 00:26:21,506
it doesn't look like it's photoshopped.

410
00:26:25,046 --> 00:26:26,876
This channel is malicious.

411
00:26:26,946 --> 00:26:29,816
A secret love affair? Does this make any sense?

412
00:26:29,876 --> 00:26:32,146
What are we going to do, Mi Young?

413
00:26:32,146 --> 00:26:33,716
What do you mean?

414
00:26:33,786 --> 00:26:35,856
It's just a baseless rumour.

415
00:26:36,316 --> 00:26:39,726
It'll probably die down after a while.

416
00:26:44,226 --> 00:26:45,296
CEO Baek.

417
00:26:47,536 --> 00:26:49,136
We need you to come see this.

418
00:26:49,536 --> 00:26:52,306
We're getting flooded with complaints from customers.

419
00:27:00,716 --> 00:27:03,116
What was just posted isn't true.

420
00:27:04,186 --> 00:27:07,316
- We're just employees... - Yes, a cancellation...

421
00:27:07,886 --> 00:27:08,956
You're cancelling...

422
00:27:10,126 --> 00:27:11,756
It's a rumour...

423
00:27:27,306 --> 00:27:29,876
Ninety percent of the clients with reservations...

424
00:27:29,936 --> 00:27:32,506
have called to cancel.

425
00:27:34,576 --> 00:27:36,516
And the other ten percent...

426
00:27:36,846 --> 00:27:39,386
said they'll think about it and get back to us.

427
00:27:45,056 --> 00:27:48,796
Maybe I should just sue that YouTuber?

428
00:27:49,526 --> 00:27:52,666
Spreading rumours like this without confirming a single fact...

429
00:27:52,766 --> 00:27:54,166
is defamation.

430
00:27:54,436 --> 00:27:57,106
But if you sue that YouTuber,

431
00:27:57,166 --> 00:27:59,106
they'll just dig into your private life...

432
00:27:59,166 --> 00:28:00,236
even more relentlessly.

433
00:28:01,976 --> 00:28:03,236
And what if...

434
00:28:03,336 --> 00:28:06,306
they find out you're in the middle of a divorce?

435
00:28:07,216 --> 00:28:08,876
Wouldn't the fallout be even worse?

436
00:28:17,956 --> 00:28:19,486
I'll leave you two alone.

437
00:28:32,066 --> 00:28:34,676
I'm sorry. This must be a big shock.

438
00:28:35,506 --> 00:28:38,376
No, these things happen.

439
00:28:40,876 --> 00:28:41,946
Look...

440
00:28:43,446 --> 00:28:47,186
No matter what anyone says, I don't care.

441
00:28:48,416 --> 00:28:49,686
Because I trust you.

442
00:28:50,656 --> 00:28:54,626
I know you would never betray me when it comes to other men.

443
00:28:55,956 --> 00:28:57,166
I'm certain of that.

444
00:28:58,466 --> 00:28:59,726
Even if you don't trust me.

445
00:29:00,296 --> 00:29:01,296
Really?

446
00:29:02,936 --> 00:29:04,366
Thank you for trusting me.

447
00:29:06,036 --> 00:29:09,106
But seriously, who could have taken this picture?

448
00:29:09,676 --> 00:29:11,506
What kind of psycho would do this?

449
00:29:13,276 --> 00:29:16,346
I don't know if "psycho" is...

450
00:29:16,646 --> 00:29:18,286
the right word...

451
00:29:18,346 --> 00:29:19,746
Of course it is.

452
00:29:26,356 --> 00:29:27,526
Could it be...

453
00:29:29,656 --> 00:29:30,996
Hee Ju?

454
00:29:32,266 --> 00:29:33,596
Did Hee Ju take the photo?

455
00:29:33,896 --> 00:29:34,896
I mean...

456
00:29:35,696 --> 00:29:38,866
I didn't know she would post it online.

457
00:29:38,936 --> 00:29:41,206
So you already knew...

458
00:29:41,276 --> 00:29:43,646
that she took the picture? Since when?

459
00:29:45,376 --> 00:29:46,776
For a while...

460
00:29:48,646 --> 00:29:49,776
Unbelievable.

461
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:01,556
If I'd really been serious about it,

462
00:30:01,926 --> 00:30:02,926
she...

463
00:30:03,626 --> 00:30:04,726
would be dead.

464
00:30:05,826 --> 00:30:08,336
But that won't happen now.

465
00:30:09,096 --> 00:30:12,266
Everything's going to be all right now, Mi Young.

466
00:30:13,736 --> 00:30:14,876
Hee Ju...

467
00:30:16,306 --> 00:30:18,746
Where is Hee Ju right now?

468
00:30:18,976 --> 00:30:21,816
- What? - I said, where is she?

469
00:30:21,946 --> 00:30:24,546
How should I know? I blocked her number.

470
00:30:24,616 --> 00:30:26,346
Call her and check, quickly.

471
00:30:26,416 --> 00:30:29,156
Why? What's with the sudden urgency?

472
00:30:30,156 --> 00:30:32,586
You want to find Hee Ju and throw her in jail, don't you?

473
00:30:32,656 --> 00:30:34,456
Stop talking nonsense and do it.

474
00:30:34,556 --> 00:30:36,226
All right.

475
00:30:36,896 --> 00:30:39,666
I have to unblock her first.

476
00:30:50,676 --> 00:30:53,076
(CEO Calvin Kim)

477
00:31:14,196 --> 00:31:15,436
Take this.

478
00:31:17,236 --> 00:31:18,566
This...

479
00:31:18,706 --> 00:31:20,706
When I gave birth to Mi Young,

480
00:31:20,876 --> 00:31:23,206
Mi Young's father gave this to me as a gift.

481
00:31:24,946 --> 00:31:27,316
Why would you give me something so precious?

482
00:31:27,376 --> 00:31:30,486
That's why I'm giving it to you. Because it's so precious.

483
00:31:34,216 --> 00:31:35,386
Thank you.

484
00:31:35,816 --> 00:31:38,756
For being such a strong source of support for Mi Young.

485
00:31:39,726 --> 00:31:42,326
Please continue to take good care of Mi Young.

486
00:31:43,596 --> 00:31:44,596
Yes.

487
00:31:45,226 --> 00:31:46,366
Don't worry.

488
00:31:47,066 --> 00:31:48,836
I promise I'll protect Mi Young.

489
00:31:53,876 --> 00:31:54,936
Wait.

490
00:31:57,906 --> 00:31:59,206
Take this with you.

491
00:32:01,616 --> 00:32:04,946
My mom gave this to you, so you should keep it.

492
00:32:06,016 --> 00:32:07,186
And...

493
00:32:07,816 --> 00:32:10,456
thank you for remembering the anniversary.

494
00:32:30,006 --> 00:32:31,006
Yes?

495
00:32:31,176 --> 00:32:32,576
Sir, I found him.

496
00:32:45,886 --> 00:32:46,886
Sir?

497
00:33:01,176 --> 00:33:02,176
Hey.

498
00:33:13,416 --> 00:33:15,616
Who are you?

499
00:33:23,596 --> 00:33:24,796
What do you think you're doing?

500
00:33:37,946 --> 00:33:38,946
Secretary Kim.

501
00:33:44,746 --> 00:33:46,246
Wait. Please, spare me.

502
00:33:47,716 --> 00:33:50,856
Why are you doing this to me?

503
00:33:58,396 --> 00:34:02,096
Please, spare me.

504
00:34:03,266 --> 00:34:04,266
Who was it?

505
00:34:07,236 --> 00:34:08,506
Who put you up to this?

506
00:34:14,446 --> 00:34:16,716
How could he not even show up on the day I'm discharged?

507
00:34:16,976 --> 00:34:20,286
He won't be showing up from now on, either.

508
00:34:20,556 --> 00:34:21,556
What did you say?

509
00:34:21,656 --> 00:34:22,686
Won Ho...

510
00:34:23,556 --> 00:34:25,256
isn't going to see you anymore, Hee Ju.

511
00:34:26,086 --> 00:34:29,096
What? He's never going to see me again?

512
00:34:33,966 --> 00:34:35,896
(My Love, Won Ho)

513
00:34:44,906 --> 00:34:46,406
Is Hee Ju still not answering her phone?

514
00:34:46,476 --> 00:34:49,816
It keeps ringing, but I think she's ignoring my calls.

515
00:34:50,146 --> 00:34:52,086
Do you have any idea where she could be?

516
00:34:52,146 --> 00:34:53,546
A close friend's place or...

517
00:34:53,616 --> 00:34:55,986
maybe a favourite spot she hangs out at.

518
00:34:56,056 --> 00:34:58,726
I contacted Man Ju, and she said she doesn't know.

519
00:34:58,786 --> 00:35:00,286
As for her favourite spot...

520
00:35:00,356 --> 00:35:03,626
There's a whiskey bar she frequents, but it's not open yet.

521
00:35:03,896 --> 00:35:04,966
Is that it?

522
00:35:05,026 --> 00:35:07,196
I don't know that much about her either.

523
00:35:08,666 --> 00:35:10,436
But really, why are you acting like this?

524
00:35:10,706 --> 00:35:13,766
It's not like she's in danger again like when she went to that cliff.

525
00:35:14,676 --> 00:35:16,736
She could be in more danger than when she was on that cliff.

526
00:35:17,136 --> 00:35:19,246
- What? - Call her again.

527
00:35:19,246 --> 00:35:20,946
Hurry. Call her again.

528
00:35:21,076 --> 00:35:22,376
Okay, I will.

529
00:35:30,526 --> 00:35:32,786
(Jihwaja Motel)

530
00:35:33,086 --> 00:35:34,256
Oh, for goodness' sake...

531
00:35:34,326 --> 00:35:35,356
Yes, welcome.

532
00:35:35,496 --> 00:35:36,496
What?

533
00:35:36,796 --> 00:35:37,826
Hello.

534
00:35:38,026 --> 00:35:39,626
Wait, what are you doing here?

535
00:35:39,996 --> 00:35:41,396
I'd like a room.

536
00:35:41,796 --> 00:35:42,796
What? A room?

537
00:35:44,306 --> 00:35:45,306
By yourself?

538
00:35:45,936 --> 00:35:47,776
Yes. Is that possible?

539
00:35:48,476 --> 00:35:50,336
Well, I don't really want to,

540
00:35:50,436 --> 00:35:52,246
but I can't be picky about my customers.

541
00:35:52,776 --> 00:35:53,946
So yes, it's possible.

542
00:35:55,976 --> 00:35:59,146
Also, can I pay for a month in advance?

543
00:35:59,846 --> 00:36:00,886
A whole month?

544
00:36:02,216 --> 00:36:03,216
Well...

545
